[<<cite:KacWak89,KacWak08>>]

The number $k$ is admissible if and only if

\begin{align*}
k+h\che=\frac{p}{q}
\quad \text{with }p,q\in \N,\ (p,q)=1,\ p\geq
\begin{cases}
h\che&\text{if }(r\che, q)=1\\
h&\text{if }(r\che,q)=r\che,
\end{cases}
\end{align*}

where
$h$ is
the Coxeter number of $\fing$.

If this is the case
we have
$\wh{\Pi}(k\Lam_0)=\{\dot{\alpha_0},\alpha_1,\alpha_2,\dots,\alpha_l\}$,
where

\begin{align*}
\dot{\alpha_0}=
\begin{cases}
-\theta+q\delta&\text{if }(r\che,q)=1
\\
-\theta_s+\frac{q}{r\che}\delta&\text{if }(r\che ,q)=r\che.
\end{cases}
\end{align*}
